      },
      "text": "After breakfast, departure to Mucubají Lagoon. Optional horseback ride to Laguna Negra.\n\nContinue to the Los Llanos region.\n\nLos Llanos — vast savannas in central Venezuela — are a true wildlife sanctuary and one of the largest bird reserves in South America.\n\nThe area is home to about 350 bird species and nearly 50 species of mammals.\n\nGuests can enjoy land and water safaris with professional guides. You’ll see Orinoco crocodiles (up to 9 meters long), feed caimans (babas) with meat, and possibly encounter anteaters, red howler monkeys, tapirs, sloths, and deer. With some luck, you may even spot ocelots or pumas.\n\nA traditional highlight is piranha fishing (Caribe Ojo Rojo) from a boat.\n\nReturn to the lodge and dinner.\n\nMeals: light breakfast, lunch, dinner"
    },
